--- !u!114 &1051019792
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1051019790}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "THE TRUCK IS THE BAG\nDrive down the ramp into the trampoline. Your speed,
    position and heading determine the launch. There is no launch button. Learn the
    reference stripes; try 13\u201314 m/s at the bed. Slow entries undershoot, fast
    or angled entries can miss.\n\nCONTROLS\nForward accelerates; opposite input
    brakes before reversing. Left/right steer. Whole controller: left stick steer,
    RT forward, LT reverse. Shared controller: one truck per left/right stick. Keyboard
    clusters shown in setup. Esc / assigned Start pauses all courses without losing
    flight or scores.\n\nAIRBORNE\nLeft/right gives a limited lateral nudge and bank.
    Release forward/back after launch, then press again for a small range/pitch correction.
    The budget is shared across directions: you cannot hover or reverse flight. First
    board contact disables all controls. Landings, skids and collisions are physical.\n\nCAB
    AND REPLAY\nEvery player starts in the driver seat, with a stable horizon. After
    a throw settles, REPLAY opens a visual recording. ANGLE cycles cab, chase, board
    side and overhead; SPEED cycles 0.25x / 0.5x / 1x / 2x / 4x. RESTART rewinds;
    LIVE CAB returns. Replays affect only your view, never physics or scores. Your
    next delivery waits while you review (45-second limit); other courses keep playing.\n\nARCADE
    FREE-FOR-ALL \xB7 NO CANCELLATION\nFive rounds, four fresh trucks per participant
    each round. Each participant has an isolated course. Earlier trucks stay on the
    board and can be pushed off (lose 1) or through the hole (become 3). Board points
    remain PROVISIONAL until the round finishes.\n\n1 POINT: stable support on the
    TOP of the board, no surrounding-ground contact. 3 POINTS: the complete truck
    passes DOWN through the opening, counted once and collected below. 0: off board,
    ground contact, side-face hangs or still moving at the generous resolution limit.
    A truck hanging in the opening only scores 1 if genuinely supported and settled.\n\nCourses
    progress independently. After everyone's fourth truck and settling, round points
    are banked. Highest total after round five wins; equal totals tie. Rematch retains
    names, input sources and difficulty. No hot seat, networking or powerups."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -7304394381272760782, guid: 8e8f97682e668e94cb30d2e6b8e13d84,
    type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
  m_fontMaterials: []
